  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#20927\", \"PowerToys#530\", \"PowerToys#22416\"], \"answer\": \"This request has been filed several times before: sharing a region of a large or ultrawide monitor in Teams. PowerToys does not offer it today. The earlier tickets were closed as duplicates of the general tracking issues (#279 and #2774, and more recently #43464), so follow the request there and add your vote. Past tickets also say that a Teams-only feature will not be built in PowerToys, and that the better fix is for Teams itself to support sharing a custom screen area (they link to a Teams feedback item for this). In the meantime, the tickets suggest the free third-party tool RegionToShare, which lets you share a region of the screen and swap apps in and out of it. Another workaround is to share a single app window, or to lower the display resolution to 1080p before presenting.\"}",
